        "original_id": "8daaf8f6-bd7c-55be-949c-d4ed1f12c2a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fredric March, Charles Laughton, Elsa Lanchester, Frances Drake, Victor Hugo, Martha Scott, Beulah Bondi, Gene Lockhart, Elisabeth Fraser\n- Films: Les Misérables (1935 film), One Foot in Heaven\n- Roles: Eponine\n- Topics: American drama films, biographical films, marriage and family\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Charles Laughton was cast in a play with his future wife Elsa Lanchester, and they lived and worked together until his death.\n- Charles Laughton and Elsa Lanchester had no children.\n- Les Misérables is a 1935 American drama film starring Fredric March and Charles Laughton.\n- Les Misérables is based on Victor Hugo's novel of the same name.\n- Frances Drake, born on October 22, 1912 and died on January 18, 2000, was an American actress.\n- Frances Drake was best known for playing Eponine in Les Misérables (1935).\n- One Foot in Heaven is a 1941 American biographical film starring Fredric March, Martha Scott, Beulah Bondi, Gene Lockhart, and Elisabeth Fraser.",
